   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to a license\nto sell liquor at retail for consumption on certain premises",
    "basePrintNo": "S7124",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7124-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §64, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7124\n\nSPONSOR: PARKER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to a\nlicense to sell liquor at retail for consumption on certain premises\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill will allow for a restaurant, Golden Blue Bar & Restaurant Inc,\nto obtain a full liquor license. The bill will amend the ABC 200-foot\nLaw which will authorize the issuing of a retail liquor license to this\nbusiness in the County of Kings, that is within a two-hundred-foot prox-\nimity of a religious teaching institution.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Is amended to authorize the issuance for a retail license for\nGolden Blue Bar & Restaurants at its current location.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nGolden Blue Bar & Restaurant Inc. applied for a liquor license which\ntook a long time to process due to the pandemic and was later denied.\nDue to the existing ABC 200-foot law, this establishment has been\nrestricted in fully serving its customers which makes it a challenge to\ncompete, thus impacting the future of business. Further-more, the reli-\ngious institution which is within 200-feet, on 1143 Flatbush Avenue, has\nexpressed that they have no objections to the request to apply for a\nfull liquor license. An exemption to the ABC 200-foot Law would allow\nGolden Blue Bar & Restaurant Inc. to operate with a full liquor license\nthey will be able to meet the needs of the community and attract more\npatrons.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
